📌 Privacy Policy

Last updated: October 30, 2026

QuickScan - QR & Barcode (“the App”) respects the privacy of its users and is committed to protecting the information that may be collected through its use. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle information within the app.

1. Information We Collect

The App does not collect, store, or share any personally identifiable information such as your name, email or phone number.

During use, the App may access the device’s camera only to enable QR and barcode scanning. This information is processed in real time and is not saved or transmitted to external servers.

2. Permissions Used

To function properly, the App may request the following permissions:

Camera: required to scan QR codes and barcodes.

Internet access: to load ads and analytics, and when the user opens scanned links directly from the app.

These permissions are never used to collect personal data.

3. Use of Information

Information obtained from scans (such as text, links, or product numbers) is processed exclusively on the user’s device. Users may choose to copy, share, or save such data.

The App does not transmit or store this information on external servers.

4. Third-Party Services

The App shows ads through Google AdMob and uses Firebase Analytics (both from Google). They do not receive your name or contact details, but they process the data described in the section "Data processed by third-party SDKs" below.

Data processed by third-party SDKs (as declared in Google Play Data safety)

This section lists, for QuickScan, the data processed by the third-party SDKs included in the app. It matches the Data safety form of the app on Google Play.

- Google AdMob (advertising): collects and shares with Google the advertising ID / app set ID and other device identifiers, an approximate location derived from your IP address, ad interactions (impressions, clicks) and diagnostics (such as app launches and performance). Purposes: advertising, ad measurement and analytics, and fraud prevention and security. We do not receive your name or contact details from AdMob.
- Firebase Analytics (Google): app interactions (events and screens viewed), the Firebase installation ID / device identifiers, and basic device and app information. Purposes: analytics and app functionality.

Ad choices: you can reset or delete your advertising ID and opt out of ads personalisation in Android Settings > Google > Ads.
Security: data sent to these services travels encrypted in transit (HTTPS/TLS).
Data deletion: the app has no user accounts. Data stored on your device is deleted by uninstalling the app or clearing its data; for data held by Google (advertising ID, analytics), reset your advertising ID as described above or write to tll.developers.apps@gmail.com and we will help with the request.

5. Security

We are committed to protecting user security. Since no personal data is collected, the risk of exposure is minimal. However, we recommend users operate the app in a safe and responsible environment.

6. Children’s Privacy

The App can be used by children; it does not collect personal information such as names or emails. However, we encourage parents or guardians to supervise the use of the App by minors.

7. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy at any time. Any changes will be posted on this page with the updated date.

8. Contact

If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:
